#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""oh - local Odoo 19 toolbelt of the odoo-harness.

Run it from anywhere inside the project repository:

  oh env [--update]               prepare PostgreSQL, the pinned Odoo source and the Python venv
  oh check [MODULE ...] [FILE]    static checks in seconds (syntax, manifests, access CSV, Odoo 19 idioms) and,
                                  on modules, pylint-odoo warnings (--no-lint skips them)
  oh test [MODULE ...]            install modules in a disposable database and run their tests
  oh shell [-c CODE] [--db DB]    run Python in `odoo-bin shell` on a kept database (rolled back)
  oh serve [--db DB] / oh stop    run this project's Odoo server on a kept database
  oh shot PATH [PATH ...]         checked screenshots of Odoo pages in every configured language
  oh src PATTERN [--module M]     search the standard Odoo (and Enterprise) source
  oh i18n MODULE [...]            export i18n/<lang>.po from a kept database
  oh evidence [--prune [--dry-run]]  check the result records, their files and the source they match; --prune
                                  deletes stale records (and partial --tags records) a newer passed whole record of
                                  the same modules or pages supersedes; --prune-stale deletes every stale record
  oh deps [MODULE ...]            print the changed modules with their project dependencies, as paths for git diff
  oh doctor                       check the installation, runtime and deployment boundaries
  oh protect                      print the GitHub ruleset that protects the deploy branches
  oh clean                        drop this project's databases (--all-projects: every project's)

Exit codes: 0 passed, 1 failed, 2 setup error, 3 blocked (modules missing locally),
4 not verified (a required test, upgrade check, valid screen, current record or protection is missing).
"""
